language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Start with [0] and build a list by adding 5, adding 7 or taking the square root; the list must contain 2, 10 and 14 in that order, with all elements distinct, at most 60 and integer, and have length 24 ending with 14.
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..24)] of int(0..60)
$ positions of the 2 and of the 10 in the list
find p2, p10 : int(1..24)

branching on [x, p2, p10]

such that
$ the list starts with 0
x[1] = 0,
$ the list ends with 14
x[24] = 14,
$ all elements of the list are distinct
allDiff(x),
$ each element is reached from the previous one by adding 5, adding 7 or taking the square root (which must be an integer)
forAll i : int(1..23) . (x[i+1] = x[i] + 5 \/ x[i+1] = x[i] + 7 \/ x[i+1] * x[i+1] = x[i]),
$ the 2 and the 10 appear in the list, in that order, before the final 14
x[p2] = 2,
x[p10] = 10,
p2 < p10,
p10 < 24
